      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "East of town, the Borrego Valley Maneuver Area served as a World War II U.S. Navy training center with camps and airstrips.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borrego_Springs%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Palms at Indian Head, built in 1947, was a Hollywood retreat that once hosted stars like Marilyn Monroe and James Arness.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.gotoborregosprings.com/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Borrego Springs’ roots trace back to the Kumeyaay and Cahuilla tribes, who inhabited the area for thousands of years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.gotoborregosprings.com/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town experiences a dry‑summer hot desert climate, with a record high of 122 °F (50 °C) set on June 25, 1990.",
